config GPIO_AX630C
	bool "Axera AX630C (AX620E) GPIO support"
	depends on ARM64 || COMPILE_TEST
	depends on OF
	select GPIOLIB_IRQCHIP
	help
	  GPIO controllers of the Axera AX630C and the rest of the AX620E
	  family: four blocks of 32 lines that borrow DesignWare register
	  names but give every line its own 32-bit control word, so GPIO_DWAPB
	  cannot drive them.

	  Say Y if you are building a kernel for an AX620E-family SoC. There is
	  no module option: on these boards the HDMI receiver's power rails,
	  the Ethernet PHY reset and the host's ATX power lines are all GPIO
	  consumers that probe long before a module could be loaded.
